-- Ministry of Ports, Shipping and Waterways. Deepened 2026-09-04 (depth
-- pass — see docs/DEPTH_PASS_PLAN.md) beyond the original bounded pass (3
-- pairs). Generated from the research log by a one-off script (scratchpad
-- gen_mopsw.py) to avoid transcription error across ~120 rows; every row
-- traces to a verbatim Full Text quote in that log. The tracker's complete
-- 216-notification MoPSW listing was enumerated and every detail page's
-- Full Text read; two Hindi-only corrigenda and one truncated preamble
-- were read from the official egazette.gov.in PDF ('primary-source-
-- egazette' tier). No "Ministry of Shipping" (pre-2020) listing exists on
-- the tracker, so pre-2023 targets are cited-only nodes taken from the
-- citing text, as the first pass already did for G.S.R. 641(E).
--
-- ~45 new chains across five subject areas:
--   A. Inland Vessels Act, 2021 rule families — all five 7 June 2022
--      principals each got a draft amendment (2024-25) and a final
--      (May 2025); plus Design & Construction (draft, final, draft,
--      final), Central Database, Prior Approval, and two pending Manning
--      drafts. Drafts are modeled `cites` in both directions of the
--      draft->final cycle (a draft has no legal effect), the final
--      `amends` the principal per its own trailing Note. The already-
--      modeled Safe Navigation pair gained its draft precursor.
--   B. Major Port Authorities Act, 2021 board-seat supersession chains
--      for eleven major ports — a "partial modification of the
--      Notification ... G.S.R. No. X(E)" variant is modeled `amends`;
--      several seats branch (one target superseded twice by different
--      seat-holders). The already-modeled Chennai chain gained its 2022
--      root. Two Hindi-only Adjudicatory Board corrigenda read from PDF.
--   C. Petroleum Rules, 2002 r.16(1) port-of-import "in continuation of
--      ... hereby extends" chains for nine ports — modeled `cites` (an
--      extension of validity, not an amendment of text; same choice as
--      Petroleum's kerosene extension), with one trailing explicit
--      supersession (Magdalla) modeled `supersedes`.
--   D. Merchant Shipping Act, 1958: a draft->final pair, a fishing-vessel
--      registrars amendment, a Seafarers Tribunal corrigendum, and the
--      Seamen's PF Board of Trustees note-chain.
--   E. Indian Ports Act 2025 (two draft->final), Indian Ports Act 1908 (a
--      partial withdrawal, modeled `rescinds`), Coastal Shipping Act 2025,
--      Marine Aids to Navigation Act 2021 (two draft->final plus a bare
--      "Notification No. 681" tenure extension), Recycling of Ships Rules
--      (bare "G.S.R. 20" principal).
--
-- REAL CITATION COLLISIONS within this ministry, all kept distinct by
-- year-suffixed gazette_id: G.S.R. 155(E) 2025/2026 (the 2026 one already
-- modeled); 347(E) 2024/2025; 333(E) 2024/2026; 395(E) 2025/2026; 217(E)
-- 2023/2024; 262(E) 2022/2025; 671/672/673(E) 2024 (IV drafts) vs 2026
-- (Merchant Shipping rules, not modeled — title-only supersessions).
--
-- REAL CITING-TEXT ERRORS kept as observed: G.S.R. 391(E) cites its
-- target G.S.R. 482(E) as "dated 06th January, 2024" — the real 482(E)
-- is 6 August 2024 (the person named matches); modeled to the real
-- document. gazettetracker's listing title for G.S.R. 677(E) says
-- "G.S.R. No. 621 E" while its text says 651(E) — titles lie.
--
-- Real leads NOT modeled: 25+ Merchant Shipping Act, 2025 rule-sets
-- (May-Sept 2026) that supersede their 1960-2016 predecessors by title
-- only — including G.S.R. 379(E) superseding the National Shipping Board
-- Rules, 1960 that the existing thread 3 sits under; nine Recruitment
-- Rules likewise; Hindi Salahkar Samiti resolutions citing predecessors
-- by gazette date only; G.S.R. 773(E)'s Stenographers' LDCE corrigendum
-- whose target number appears only in the target's own text; draft-only
-- IV families with no final yet (Special Category Vessels, NRTNS,
-- Coastal Shipping Licencing, AtoN Inquiry/Penalty).


